    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.move\n\n### Description\n\nThanks for this helpful plugin!\r\n\r\nI noticed when I activate `line_left`/`line_right`, repeat is possible by pressing `.`, but it doesn't work for `line_up` and `line_down`. It would be nice if it worked for these actions as well.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua minimal.lua`\r\n2. Press `<a-j>`\r\n3. Press `.`\r\n\r\nminimal.lua:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal lazypath = '/tmp/minimal-mini.lua-bug-report/lazy/lazy.nvim'\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n  vim.fn.system({\r\n    'git',\r\n    'clone',\r\n    '--filter=blob:none',\r\n    'https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git',\r\n    '--branch=stable', -- latest stable release\r\n    lazypath,\r\n  })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\nrequire 'lazy'.setup {\r\n  {\r\n    'echasnovski/mini.move',\r\n    config = function() require 'mini.move'.setup() end,\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nFirst 3 lines to become:\r\n```lua\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n  vim.fn.system({\r\n          local lazypath = '/tmp/minimal-mini.lua-bug-report/lazy/lazy.nvim'\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nFirst 3 lines is:\r\n```lua\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n        local lazypath = '/tmp/minimal-mini.lua-bug-report/lazy/lazy.nvim'\r\n  vim.fn.system({\r\n ```",
