            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Yeah, I used `[e` and  `]e` too. Personally I think key combination is for emacs, we use vim to have key sequences and avoid hurting pinkie. Also alt/meta are not easily available on all terminal emulator. I have them on macOS (left alt is alt, right alt is for diacritics) but I know it is tricky in some terminal emulators. Btw, not a deal breaker, everybody can change the default mappings as they wish and enjoy mini.nvim, we just need repeat to work.\r\n\r\nI also have `[r` and `]r` for moving characters left and right, it would be nice if `mini.nvim` supports these too, maybe I should create another issue or maybe even a PR if it is a feature with a single user :-)",
