        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I also have `[r` and `]r` for moving characters left and right, it would be nice if `mini.nvim` supports these too, maybe I should create another issue or maybe even a PR if it is a feature with a single user :-)\r\n\r\nProbably, not the best fit in 'mini.move', as there is `move_selection()`. I'd suggest making custom keymappings:\r\n\r\n```\r\nnmap [r v<M-h>v\r\nnmap ]r v<M-l>v\r\n```\r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n- Replace `<M-h>` and `<M-l>` with your mappings for horizontal movement of visual selection.\r\n- This is not ideal as it overrides previous visual selection (`gv` will reselect moved single character). But at the moment I feel this is worthwhile trade-off.",
