        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I had these:\r\n\r\n```Lua\r\nvim.keymap.set(\r\n  'n',\r\n  ']r',\r\n  function()\r\n    vim.fn['repeat#set'](\"]r\", vim.v.count)\r\n    return '@=len([execute(\"let b:_tmp=@a\"),execute(\\'normal! \"aylx\"ap\\')' ..\r\n        ',execute(\"let @a=b:_tmp\"),execute(\"unlet b:_tmp\")]) ? \"hl\" : \"\" <cr>'\r\n  end,\r\n  { expr = true, silent = true }\r\n)\r\nvim.keymap.set(\r\n  'n',\r\n  '[r',\r\n  function()\r\n    vim.fn['repeat#set'](\"[r\", vim.v.count)\r\n    return '@=len([execute(\"let b:_tmp=@a\"),execute(\\'normal! \"ayhx\"ap\\')' ..\r\n        ',execute(\"let @a=b:_tmp\"),execute(\"unlet b:_tmp\")]) ? \"h\" : \"\" <cr>'\r\n  end,\r\n  { expr = true, silent = true }\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI don't understand what exactly I achieved in these cryptic vim script snippets, it is written years ago, but it was doing the job.\r\n\r\nYesterday I changed them to these:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set(\r\n  'n',\r\n  '[r',\r\n  function()\r\n    vim.fn['repeat#set'](\"[r\", vim.v.count)\r\n    local pos = vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\r\n    local col = pos[2]\r\n    if col <= 0 then return end\r\n    local line = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line()\r\n    vim.api.nvim_set_current_line(\r\n      line:sub(1, col - 1) .. line:sub(col + 1, col + 1) .. line:sub(col, col) .. line:sub(col + 2)\r\n    )\r\n    vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { pos[1], pos[2] - 1 })\r\n  end,\r\n  {}\r\n)\r\nvim.keymap.set(\r\n  'n',\r\n  ']r',\r\n  function()\r\n    vim.fn['repeat#set'](\"]r\", vim.v.count)\r\n    local pos = vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\r\n    local col = pos[2]\r\n    local line = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line()\r\n    vim.api.nvim_set_current_line(\r\n      line:sub(1, col) .. line:sub(col + 2, col + 2) .. line:sub(col + 1, col + 1) .. line:sub(col + 3)\r\n    )\r\n    vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { pos[1], pos[2] + 1 })\r\n  end,\r\n  {}\r\n)\r\n```",
