        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> `xp` and `Xph` are the way most people go, it just ruins the registers as you mentioned,\r\n\r\nYes, this is why I said that it needs to cache register content (and later restore). This is what id one in 'mini.move' anyway.\r\n\r\n> Btw, the trend these days is to have mini.everything ;) Maybe we can have a mini.repeat. [It is one of the smallest and yet popular vim plugins](https://github.com/tpope/vim-repeat/blob/master/autoload/repeat.vim). I couldn't believe my search for \"repeat.nvim\" or \"nvim-repeat\" in Google returned no result.\r\n\r\nYeah, I've seen those. The thing is that there is no additional benefit to just rewriting it Lua.\r\n\r\nBut you've moved me towards an idea of 'mini.keymap' which can contain something like `MiniKeymap.with_dotrepeat()` and `MiniKeymap.with_timer()` (resolving #86 which I am thinking about sometimes) for different kinds of mappings. I'll definitely think about it.",
