        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Yeah, I've seen those. The thing is that there is no additional benefit to just rewriting it Lua.\r\n\r\nWell, it can be beyond rewriting, we can add features or improve usage. One thing that bothers me in vim-repeat is that you need to write you lhs twice (once in keymap definition, and then in repeat call), then whenever you change the keymap you should be careful not to forget updating repeat call. So I have a helper function `rkeymap` which calls vim.keymap, with a wrapped version of the callback sent to it to automatically call repeat.",
