        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> So I've looked into adding dot-repeat to mappings for moving current line and it is not that simple. Usual approach of setting `'operatorfunc'` and using expression mapping doesn't work right away here. The main reason seems to be that `move_line()` itself uses some dot-repeatable actions which override the main one.\r\n> \r\n> I'll give it another go, but my hopes are not high at the moment.\r\n\r\nAs much as I would like to support this, I don't see a reasonable way to introduce dot-repeat while preserving all current functionality in edge-cases. The thing is, that latter is done by essentially `\"zdd` - `<Up>/<Down>` - `\"zP` (or `\"zp`). First and last steps are themselves dot-repeatable which breaks any my attempt to make whole function dot-repeatable.\r\n\r\nClosing as \"would love to support but don't think it is reasonably possible\".",
